  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds tests and a decision record. It changes no product code.\n\nIssue #1241 asked whether a toolpath generated and cleared on machine A can post on machine B without being checked against B. A remount happens two ways: through the setup's own machine (`SetSetupMachine`) or through the document's machine (`LoadMachine`), which the setup follows. The new suite `crates/app/tests/machine_switch.rs` traces both.\n\n**Result: only the display is stale. No path posts on B without being checked.** For every law the post checks the cached path again, against the machine the op's setup mounts now:\n\n| Law (path made on A, mounted on B) | Op status after the switch | Gate / post on B |\n|---|---|---|\n| Travel (B: +/-10 mm) | Ok | refused: `machine TightMill: ... Face1: move N reaches ... the stroke is -10.000..10.000` |\n| Spindle max rpm (B: 1000) | Ok | refused: `Face1: tool EM-0400-2FL runs ... above the machine's 1000` |\n| Rotary (tilt-head to VMC 3-axis, leaning pocket) | Ok | refused: `P: move N tilts the tool; ... states no tilting rotary` |\n| Machine kind (mill to Lathe) | Ok | refused: `Face1: a ... operation cannot run on its setup's ... machine` |\n\nEvery refusal writes no file. The same results hold through each switch route (setup and document), after undo (A is back and the program posts), after redo, and after save and reopen.\n\nThe op still reads Ok after a switch on purpose. This is the M2.3 \"roomy-one\" law: machine limits and workholding feed the post's live gate and are never part of the op stamp. It is pinned by `fixtures.rs::workholding_never_stales_a_fresh_toolpath` (\"loading a machine must not re-generate the program\"). M3.2 B once tried a machine digest term in the stamp and reverted it. So the issue's \"Done means\" is met by its \"or the issue records why it need not\" branch. `docs/decisions/1241-machine-switch-live-gate.md` records the decision, the options I dropped (stamping the machine identity, or only the fields generation reads), and what it would cost to change if the maintainer wants a switch to show ops as stale.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning tests, `crates/app/tests/machine_switch.rs` (6):\n  - `a_setups_new_machine_judges_stroke_and_spindle_at_the_post`\n  - `the_documents_new_machine_judges_stroke_and_spindle_at_the_post`\n  - `a_setups_new_machine_without_the_rotary_refuses_the_lean`\n  - `the_documents_new_machine_without_the_rotary_refuses_the_lean`\n  - `a_setups_new_machine_of_another_kind_refuses_the_family`\n  - `the_documents_new_machine_of_another_kind_refuses_the_family`\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 6 of 6.\n- Neighbouring suites: `setup_mount`, `fixtures`, `post_not_judged` and `machine` all green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The per-mount post (`post_mounts`), where setups run on different machines. It uses the same `machine_problems` gate.\n- The spindle-body and table steel after a switch. These are checked by the live fixture gate (`fixture_struck` reads the setup's current machine), and the existing fixture suites pin that.\n- The UI. The UI test comment the issue quotes (`setup_mount_pages.rs`) is not on upstream main.\n\nEffort: high (did not escalate)\nFork synced at v0.18.0; branch cut from upstream/main 37482923.\n\nChangelog: none (tests and a decision record only)\n\nFixes #1241\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
